# Collisions the help marks with ⚠ that are meant. TestCollisions fails
# on a collision this file doesn't list, and on a line no context has.
#
# One collision per line:
#
#   context | key | loser | winner | reason
#
# context names where the keys are, as keyContexts in keyctx_test.go does.
# loser is the binding that doesn't get key, and winner the one that
# does, each as "layer source: description", the way the help shows them.
# reason says in a line why the collision is meant.
#
# A binding shadowed by an earlier layer, such as the app's, needs a line
# as much as a conflict within one layer: the help marks both.

actions: jobs | [ | actions: previous pane | actions: previous tab | ] and [ switch the tabs; tab and shift+tab still move between the panes
actions: jobs | ] | actions: pane | actions: tab | ] and [ switch the tabs; tab and shift+tab still move between the panes
actions: jobs | ctrl+r | actions: refresh | actions: rerun failed | ctrl+r re-runs the failed jobs; r still refreshes
actions: jobs | f | jobs: page down | actions: filter | f opens the filter; pgdown still pages down
actions: log | [ | actions: previous pane | actions: previous tab | ] and [ switch the tabs; tab and shift+tab still move between the panes
actions: log | ] | actions: pane | actions: tab | ] and [ switch the tabs; tab and shift+tab still move between the panes
